; A motion-object geometry fixture.
;
; ORIGINAL WORK. Nothing here comes from the game source, and it is committable
; for the same reason `chill65-native/fixture/fixture.MAC` is: it is a program
; we wrote, exercising hardware we modelled.
;
; # Why it exists
;
; Sprite geometry cannot be calibrated on a recorded trace of the game. Our
; runtime and an oracle are not in the same game state during one — measured on
; `gameplay.trace`, at frame 600 our object table is parked while MAME draws
; four characters, and at frame 960 both have objects but different ones in
; different places. No sprite model can reconcile that, so the comparison says
; nothing about geometry.
;
; This program removes the game from the question. It plants a known object
; table, never touches it again, and loops. Whatever an implementation draws is
; then a function of the sprite hardware alone, and two implementations
; disagreeing have disagreed about the hardware.
;
; # What it plants
;
; Nine objects, chosen to pin one thing each:
;
;   0  mid-screen, the reference
;   1  the same picture one row down, so the vertical step is visible
;   2  x = 0 and 3  x = 248, the two horizontal extremes
;   4  x = 252, which must wrap across the right edge
;   5  MPI set over a bright bitmap pixel, which the bitmap should win
;   6  MPI set over a dim one, which the object should win
;   7  colour 0, which is opaque even under priority (see `cram_address`)
;   8  a second row of the same picture, for the vertical extent
;
; Every other entry is parked at F0 in all four bytes: a vertical position of
; F0 puts the match window at VC 00-0F, which no visible line reaches.

	.=0E000

; ---------------------------------------------------------------- entry
START::	SEI
	CLD
	LDX I,0FF
	TXS

; The OUT1 latch, one bit per address, sampling D3. Zero everything: MT.BSL
; clear selects the 8E00 table, PLAYER2 clear means no cocktail flip.
	LDA I,00
	STA 09F00
	STA 09F01
	STA 09F02
	STA 09F03
	STA 09F04
	STA 09F05
	STA 09F06
	STA 09F07

; Colour RAM. Writes land at BA[4:0] with BA[5] supplying the ninth bit, so
; 9F80+n sets entry n with bit 8 clear and 9FA0+n sets it with bit 8 set.
; Entry 16 — what a bitmap pixel of zero selects — is set to 1FF, which is
; black, because every component is active-low. The motion colours are left at
; entry 0, which decodes to white.
	LDA I,0FF
	STA 09FB0

; ---------------------------------------------------------- park the table
; All 64 entries, F0 in every byte.
	LDA I,0F0
	LDX I,00
PARK:	STA AX,08E00
	STA AX,08F00
	INX
	BNE PARK

; --------------------------------------------------------- plant the objects
; Byte 0 picture, byte 1 vertical position, byte 2 bit 7 = MPI, byte 3
; horizontal position. A vertical position of V puts the object's first row on
; the line where VC + V first reaches F0, so V = F0 - line.

; 0: picture 1 at line 64, x 64.
	LDA I,01
	STA 08E00
	LDA I,0B0
	STA 08E01
	LDA I,00
	STA 08E02
	LDA I,040
	STA 08E03

; 1: the same picture sixteen lines lower, directly beneath it.
	LDA I,01
	STA 08E04
	LDA I,0A0
	STA 08E05
	LDA I,00
	STA 08E06
	LDA I,040
	STA 08E07

; 2: hard against the left edge.
	LDA I,01
	STA 08E08
	LDA I,0B0
	STA 08E09
	LDA I,00
	STA 08E0A
	LDA I,00
	STA 08E0B

; 3: the last object fully on screen.
	LDA I,01
	STA 08E0C
	LDA I,0B0
	STA 08E0D
	LDA I,00
	STA 08E0E
	LDA I,0F8
	STA 08E0F

; 4: four pixels off the right edge, so half of it must wrap to x 0-3.
	LDA I,01
	STA 08E10
	LDA I,0B0
	STA 08E11
	LDA I,00
	STA 08E12
	LDA I,0FC
	STA 08E13

; 5: priority set, at line 96.
	LDA I,01
	STA 08E14
	LDA I,090
	STA 08E15
	LDA I,080
	STA 08E16
	LDA I,060
	STA 08E17

; 6: priority clear, beside it, so the pair differ only in MPI.
	LDA I,01
	STA 08E18
	LDA I,090
	STA 08E19
	LDA I,00
	STA 08E1A
	LDA I,070
	STA 08E1B

; 7: picture 2, whose pixels are colour 0 — opaque even under priority.
	LDA I,02
	STA 08E1C
	LDA I,090
	STA 08E1D
	LDA I,080
	STA 08E1E
	LDA I,080
	STA 08E1F

; 8: picture 3 at line 128, for a second vertical reference.
	LDA I,03
	STA 08E20
	LDA I,070
	STA 08E21
	LDA I,00
	STA 08E22
	LDA I,0A0
	STA 08E23

; ------------------------------------------------------------------ idle
; Nothing further touches the table. The watchdog is strobed so the machine
; stays alive; a board that stopped being petted would reset and the picture
; would go away.
IDLE::	STA 09E00
	JMP IDLE

; Vectors. No interrupts are taken — I is set and never cleared — but the
; vectors must exist.
	.=0FFFA
	.WORD START
	.WORD START
	.WORD START
